	"_readme": [
		"The gb16 bank's shapes at 32px: every pixel doubled, by tools/upscale_bank.py-shaped",
		"arithmetic done once and committed - this file is DATA, not output, so it can be edited.",
		"It exists so an imported style (lpc32) has terrain to stand on before the real 32px",
		"terrain arrives (M40 phase B2): the ids are gb16's, which is what lets the demo's maps",
		"load unchanged under either style. Doubled pixel art is chunkier than drawn pixel art;",
		"that is the placeholder's honest look, and the reason it is a placeholder."
